15:00.456 --> 15:02.453
I lied! I just want to be free,

15:02.454 --> 15:05.656
like a recently divorced man
with no kids!

15:08.893 --> 15:10.460
This is nice.

15:10.461 --> 15:12.302
This is better.

15:15.801 --> 15:17.468
Stewie, I can't believe it.

15:17.469 --> 15:19.637
I mean, do-do you think
Lois could be having an affair

15:19.638 --> 15:20.738
with this Horatio guy?

15:20.739 --> 15:22.407
Brian, will you watch Stewie?

15:22.408 --> 15:23.740
I have to go get groceries

15:23.741 --> 15:25.676
and won't be back until later tonight.

15:25.677 --> 15:27.311
Uh, yeah, sure.

15:27.312 --> 15:28.812
Oh, my God, Stewie,
she's going to the store

15:28.813 --> 15:30.480
and won't be back until tonight?

15:30.481 --> 15:32.215
Do you know what that means?

15:32.216 --> 15:35.018
Disguises?

15:35.019 --> 15:37.754
No, but we should follow her and
see what the hell is going on.

15:37.755 --> 15:39.089
Stewie-Chan!

15:43.494 --> 15:44.594
I'll meet you there, Brian.

15:44.595 --> 15:46.398
I've got to finish my shift.

15:53.839 --> 15:56.206
All right, Peter, now, I know
you haven't eaten in a while,

15:56.207 --> 15:59.042
so this is something called
the Pocket Diet.

15:59.043 --> 16:00.578
Okay, guys, empty your pockets.

16:00.579 --> 16:03.346
Whatever you got in there, he eats.

16:03.347 --> 16:06.716
Uh, Glenn, can we go somewhere
and just talk for a minute?

16:06.717 --> 16:07.786
Aah!

16:09.187 --> 16:10.955
Guys, stop saying things, all right?

16:10.956 --> 16:12.553
I will say the things.

16:22.868 --> 16:23.868
Oh, my God.

16:23.869 --> 16:25.204
He's getting in the car.

16:26.538 --> 16:27.705
He's going in for a hug.

16:27.706 --> 16:29.373
They're hugging! This is insane!

16:29.374 --> 16:31.242
I know. This guy.

16:31.243 --> 16:34.313
This guy is a star.

16:38.417 --> 16:40.084
I can't believe it, Stewie.
She picked him up.

16:40.085 --> 16:41.085
They hugged.

16:41.086 --> 16:42.386
Lois is having an affair.

16:42.387 --> 16:44.555
We've got to stop them.

16:44.556 --> 16:47.557
Aw, great.

16:47.558 --> 16:50.560
Just great.

17:09.614 --> 17:12.083
Lois, don't do it!

17:12.084 --> 17:13.084
Brian?

17:13.085 --> 17:14.619
What the hell are you doing here?

17:14.620 --> 17:16.086
Don't do what?

17:16.087 --> 17:17.255
Don't have sex with Horatio!

17:17.256 --> 17:18.421
It's not worth it!

17:18.422 --> 17:19.690
What are you talking about?

17:19.691 --> 17:21.825
Look, I found your book and read it.

17:21.826 --> 17:23.427
I thought that you wrote

17:23.428 --> 17:25.095
everything you were looking for
in a lover,

17:25.096 --> 17:27.931
and, if I could embody some
of those things,

17:27.932 --> 17:30.200
maybe I would have a shot with you.

17:30.201 --> 17:31.935
But then I found out Horatio is real,

17:31.936 --> 17:34.104
and-and I couldn't bear to see
you do something like this

17:34.105 --> 17:35.539
to the family.

17:35.540 --> 17:37.374
It's not you, Lois.

17:37.375 --> 17:39.442
Wait, let me get this straight.

17:39.443 --> 17:42.113
You, without asking,
read something I wrote?

17:42.114 --> 17:43.847
Then, thinking I was revealing

17:43.848 --> 17:46.183
all my most intimate wants and desires,

17:46.184 --> 17:47.684
you thought that you could exploit

17:47.685 --> 17:49.953
what you read to seduce me?

17:49.954 --> 17:51.822
But when you thought I might be cheating

17:51.823 --> 17:53.324
with someone other than yourself,

17:53.325 --> 17:56.326
you found that, and only that,
morally objectionable?

17:56.327 --> 17:57.995
And you bring Stewie here,

17:57.996 --> 18:00.064
who doesn't understand any of this?!

18:00.065 --> 18:02.533
I predict, in the finale,
everyone can understand me.

18:02.534 --> 18:04.235
That'd make a good finale, right?

18:04.236 --> 18:06.069
Brian, this is Horatio.

18:06.070 --> 18:07.805
He's special.

18:07.806 --> 18:09.574
I know you think he's special.

18:09.575 --> 18:10.975
No, he's special.

18:10.976 --> 18:12.809
He's learning disabled.

18:12.810 --> 18:15.179
I like Coldplay.

18:15.180 --> 18:17.315
- Ooh...
- Oh...

18:17.316 --> 18:19.482
I'm not having an affair
with him, Brian.

18:19.483 --> 18:22.085
I volunteered at the special
needs living facility,

18:22.086 --> 18:24.221
and Horatio happened to like horses.

18:24.222 --> 18:26.390
So, once a week,
I take him to the stables.

18:26.391 --> 18:29.559
And the cape is from a Darth
Vader costume he had as a kid.

18:29.560 --> 18:32.028
Did you know he's the boss
of the stormtroopers?

18:32.029 --> 18:34.664
Yes, I have fantasies
about him dominating me

18:34.665 --> 18:35.999
with his idiot strength.

18:36.000 --> 18:37.335
But it's just that...

18:37.336 --> 18:38.702
A fantasy.

18:38.703 --> 18:40.438
That's why I wrote it in a story,

18:40.439 --> 18:43.440
because I knew
that I would never act on it.

18:43.441 --> 18:45.042
Ugh. I never thought a dog

18:45.043 --> 18:47.711
could be such a genuine piece
of human garbage.

18:47.712 --> 18:49.046
Lois,

18:49.047 --> 18:51.248
I'm truly sorry for what I thought.

18:51.249 --> 18:53.584
It all just made sense to me
at the time.

18:53.585 --> 18:55.920
But now that I see what it is,

18:55.921 --> 18:58.055
I'm ashamed of myself.

18:58.056 --> 18:59.923
I hope you can find it in your heart...

18:59.924 --> 19:01.259
Hey, Bri.

19:02.893 --> 19:04.544
There's a good girl.

19:08.066 --> 19:09.133
Joe and Cleveland,

19:09.134 --> 19:11.370
are you ready to see your new Peter?

19:16.107 --> 19:19.043
What do you guys think?

19:19.044 --> 19:20.377
I don't believe it.

19:20.378 --> 19:21.778
I'm speechless.

19:23.781 --> 19:26.730
Hey, look, it's Jonah Hill sometimes!

19:33.557 --> 19:34.892
Wow!

19:34.893 --> 19:36.893
Looking good, Peter.

19:36.894 --> 19:39.563
Yes. I might want me
a little taste of that.

19:39.564 --> 19:41.565
Oh, well, Sheila, look out.

19:41.566 --> 19:43.800
Be careful what you ask for,
'cause you never know...

19:43.801 --> 19:45.670
I might... Are-are you serious?

19:45.671 --> 19:47.270
'Cause I will do this, 100%.

19:47.271 --> 19:48.471
My wife's in, too. I'll call her.

19:48.472 --> 19:50.007
We'll do a whole thing.

19:50.008 --> 19:52.677
Hey, Lois, I got a two-top.

19:52.678 --> 19:53.744
Okay.

19:53.745 --> 19:55.748
She's out, but I'm still in.

20:00.951 --> 20:02.319
Boy, I got to admit,

20:02.320 --> 20:03.921
I feel a little sheepish
to get so fooled

20:03.922 --> 20:06.123
by a silly little book that Lois wrote.

20:06.124 --> 20:08.425
Yes, but, you know, I think
what we missed in all of this

20:08.426 --> 20:11.862
is that Lois wrote a beginning,
middle, and end to something.

20:11.863 --> 20:13.530
What have you written lately, Brian?

20:13.531 --> 20:15.498
Well, nothing, but, you know,
I think-I think

20:15.499 --> 20:17.133
any writer knows how hard it is

20:17.134 --> 20:18.768
to be staring at that blank page.

20:18.769 --> 20:21.104
Sounds like you did write something:

20:21.105 --> 20:22.773
your career's obituary.

20:24.009 --> 20:26.376
Well, that's our dog and baby.

20:26.377 --> 20:28.278
Hi, this is Chris Griffin.

20:28.279 --> 20:31.281
Boy, Lois had some
amorous adventures this week.

20:31.282 --> 20:33.517
<i>But you know what really turns me on?</i>

20:33.518 --> 20:34.852
Reading.

20:34.853 --> 20:36.787
Why don't you get yourself
down to the library

20:36.788 --> 20:38.288
and open up a book.

20:38.289 --> 20:40.524
Here's a few of my favorite books.

20:40.525 --> 20:42.727
<i>J.D. Salinger's Catcher in the Rye.</i>

20:42.728 --> 20:45.395
<i>The Kite Runner by Khaled Hosseini.</i>

20:45.396 --> 20:48.132
<i>And, of course, The Dirt by Motley Crue.</i>

20:48.133 --> 20:50.200
<i>Seriously, read The Dirt.</i>

20:50.201 --> 20:52.969
They snort a row of live ants
like cocaine.

20:52.970 --> 20:55.672
Remember, kids, a library card is free,

20:55.673 --> 20:57.975
but knowledge is priceless.

20:57.976 --> 20:59.982
<i>Get that Dirt book.</i>

20:59.983 --> 21:03.983
Thank you for watching "Family Guy" on
www.FOX-fan.tv